From: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:07:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: realtek-otto: avoid synchronous IRQ disable

Restart handlers run from an atomic notifier chain and are expected to
restart the machine immediately. Calling disable_irq() from the Realtek
Otto restart handler violates that contract because it may sleep while
waiting for an active IRQ handler to finish.

This can deadlock reboot on MIPS. The architecture stops secondary CPUs
before invoking restart handlers, so a phase 1 handler which was active
on a stopped CPU can never finish. The watchdog reset is never armed and
the remaining CPU eventually reports RCU stalls.

Use disable_irq_nosync() instead. There is no need to wait for an old
phase 1 handler when the watchdog is immediately reprogrammed to reset
the SoC.

Signed-off-by: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
---
 drivers/watchdog/realtek_otto_wdt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/watchdog/realtek_otto_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/realtek_otto_wdt.c
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@ static int otto_wdt_restart(struct watch
 	u32 reset_mode;
 	u32 v;
 
-	disable_irq(ctrl->irq_phase1);
+	disable_irq_nosync(ctrl->irq_phase1);
 
 	switch (reboot_mode) {
 	case REBOOT_SOFT:
